Chapter: DeskNoticeTest
  cites Works chapter GopDesk
  cites Foreword chapter Console

 The taskbar notice lasts dk-notice-secs DISTINCT seconds. Second 11 is taken
 twice, the way a pane repaint re-takes the clock inside one second, and must
 cost one second, not two: the row that reads blank at second 15 and shows
 the notice at 14 is what that decides. The first row is the control that an
 unset notice answers blank.

Section: Walk

  seconds : List Integer = [10, 11, 11, 12, 13, 14, 15]

  walk : Integer, List Integer, Integer, Text -> Text
  walk (ds) (xs) (i) (acc) =
    if i >= list-length xs then acc
    else let now = list-at xs i
    in let t = dk-notice-take ds now
    in walk ds xs (i + 1) (acc & " " & show now & "=" & (if text-length t == 0 then "-" else t))

Section: Entry

  opening : [Console] Nothing
  opening = act
    let ds = alloc-zeroed dk-ds-bytes 64
    in let i = dk-notice-init ds
    in let before = dk-notice-take ds 9
    in let s = dk-notice-set ds "shot SH1.BMP ok"
    in act
      print-line-uni ("unset: " & (if text-length before == 0 then "blank" else before))
      print-line-uni ("clock invalidated: " & show (peek-32 ds desk-second-cell))
      print-line-uni ("walk:" & walk ds seconds 0 "")
      let long = dk-notice-set ds "0123456789012345678901234567890123456789012345678901234567890123456789"
      in print-line-uni ("long kept " & show (text-length (dk-notice-take ds 20)) & " of 70")
    end
  end
